    },
    {
      "sha": "ccb34f4d449dcfb1736918e35a737e102914c6d2",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/ccb34f4d449dcfb1736918e35a737e102914c6d2",
      "message": "Merge branch 'p1/r10-publishable' into p1/land6a",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-28T10:39:06Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "0696d5916f2f528960d4b74a41d01cced98a7c90",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/0696d5916f2f528960d4b74a41d01cced98a7c90",
      "message": "Check each retention scan page size in its own test\n\nThe whole-store cycle is computed once; each page size then replays the\nstore and compares, so no single test runs four full cycles.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-28T05:57:45Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "0eab46b3e6d5ba5e6c2bbb3d5681a3313b1f6911",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/0eab46b3e6d5ba5e6c2bbb3d5681a3313b1f6911",
      "message": "Keep the deployment refusal test off the transaction-flow guard\n\nThe refusal stops the node before it submits anything, so the guard's\ncheck that every confirmed transaction reached the follower store has\nnothing to see when the fixture is replayed.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-28T04:43:12Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "82a31360e313410f55d3a849db8646eeadebbd6e",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/82a31360e313410f55d3a849db8646eeadebbd6e",
      "message": "Register the public testnet parameter table as a generated doc channel",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-28T04:43:12Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "cd456dc6bfe2e47a7cf8dbbb739db0b86c987b59",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/cd456dc6bfe2e47a7cf8dbbb739db0b86c987b59",
      "message": "Close the remaining gaps in the SDK publish-set check\n\npnpm skips postpack when a pack fails, so a failed pack left the\nrepository LICENSE and validation's vendored copy in the package. The\ncheck now removes them itself whatever the pack does, and\ndemo/midgard-validation/vendor/ is ignored.\n\nThe type probe dropped every tsc line outside the probe files and the\npublish set's declarations, so a failure that named no such file (a\nmissing @types/node, a crash) passed. Errors that name no file are now\nreported, a failure that printed no error is reported with its output\ntail, and an @types/node the probe cannot link is a problem.\n\nThe probe now runs TypeScript 5.8 (the SDK's typescript-5-8 dev\ndependency), the first compiler that lets a CommonJS consumer require\nthe packages' ES module dependencies; the packages declare Node.js\n22.12.0 or newer, and the release doc and package READMEs say both.\n\nValidation ships modified MPL-2.0 code, so its licence is\nApache-2.0 AND MPL-2.0 and the pack writes a SOURCE.md beside the\nvendored copy that names where the modified source is; the check\nrequires it. The release doc also says that any app loading validation\nat runtime must declare the forestry itself, and that registry\nconsumers get the unpatched blake2b.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-28T03:55:53Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "0ee67ae56be33de808e5c6346d75154a45f9c79b",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/0ee67ae56be33de808e5c6346d75154a45f9c79b",
      "message": "Make the watcher declare the Merkle Patricia Forestry it loads at runtime\n\nValidation resolves #merkle-patricia-forestry to the workspace package but lists it only as a dev dependency, and the watcher listed it as a dev dependency too, so its pnpm deploy --prod image reached the package only through pnpm's hidden hoist. Declare it in the watcher's dependencies with the specifier the node, the DA committee node and fault proofs use.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-28T03:55:42Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "fad34ca92c6dcfa8db668b4239a2bee143a35cac",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/fad34ca92c6dcfa8db668b4239a2bee143a35cac",
      "message": "Merge branch 'p1/r10-r3' into p1/land5",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-28T03:26:05Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "c523ab2e48edf2fa930a6107464c804229c5fb48",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/c523ab2e48edf2fa930a6107464c804229c5fb48",
      "message": "Report an SDK invalid-UTxO refusal as a node deposit error",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-28T03:25:59Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "c05d98223d9c16a525ee35ec82d26692a3b992c6",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/c05d98223d9c16a525ee35ec82d26692a3b992c6",
      "message": "Merge branch 'p1/r10-r3' into p1/land5",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-28T03:25:09Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "7c3eafb987ee2db4c588ec8d58d0a45c4feec3ee",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/7c3eafb987ee2db4c588ec8d58d0a45c4feec3ee",
      "message": "Make the SDK packages publishable\n\nThe publish check failed on the real packages. Each tarball now installs\nfrom the registry by itself:\n\n- Core no longer depends on the private native transport. The node\n  readers that need it (reward accounts, the Kupmios ledger and the\n  protocol-parameter snapshot) move to midgard-l1-follower, which the\n  tools that use them already depend on. Type-only assertions keep the\n  core sources they reach valid under the follower's stricter settings;\n  core's emitted JavaScript is unchanged.\n- Validation imports its patched Merkle Patricia Forestry through\n  #merkle-patricia-forestry. In the workspace that is the package\n  installed from the vendored tarball; the pack copies that package into\n  the tarball and the published import points at the copy, so the\n  registry package runs the vendored code. Its dependencies become\n  validation's own.\n- publishConfig gives each package its registry exports: no\n  midgard-source condition, no test-only exports, and .d.cts types for\n  every require target. Core publishes no imports.\n- Every tarball carries the repository LICENSE, copied in only while it\n  is packed, and leaves out the local build stamps in dist/.\n- Core's declarations name the budget table as a type, not as a\n  JavaScript value.\n- The SDK lists core once.\n\nThe check now requires each packed export to be the registry form of\nits workspace export, the LICENSE, an exact vendored copy, and no hidden\nfiles.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-28T03:25:07Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "5b776d7160c80607a921000102738e357a005576",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/5b776d7160c80607a921000102738e357a005576",
      "message": "Let the node deposit builder report an invalid UTxO from the SDK",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-28T02:22:52Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "9d666336bfe58a3bc1414ca9927063f3652c20a9",
